### Justification
The fact-check found that while New Brunswick's Education Minister announced schools would resume in September 2020, the available sources—dated June and July 2020—only confirm planning and preparation for a reopening, with the specific format (in-person, online, or hybrid) undetermined and contingent on the evolving pandemic situation. No evidence was presented to confirm that schools had actually resumed operations in any format by the claim date of September 8, 2020, making the claim unsupported by the documented facts.